1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,180
She's my sister, Mini.

3
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:29,340
Interesting.

4
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:34,110
My sister lent you her Yo-Yo the other day,

5
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,580
and you just walked off like that?

6
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,020
Everyone, listen up.

7
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:38,460
We're not here for a vacation.

8
00:01:38,920 --> 00:01:39,420
And this isn't a spa retreat.

9
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:41,340
We are here to train!

10
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:42,780
Take all that off right now!

11
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:47,100
Shawn! What are you doing here?

12
00:01:47,560 --> 00:01:48,540
What's a Yo-Yo, anyway?

13
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:50,940
It's just a ball on a string.

14
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:53,340
Now what?

15
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:56,220
Hmph. Just you wait.

16
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:59,500
Episode 6

17
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:15,900
Look! A huge lotus pond!

18
00:02:17,320 --> 00:02:20,700
Leo, what made you suddenly decide to join the school Team?

19
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:22,620
Leo!

20
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:24,990
I wonder if there are squirrels here.

21
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,460
I'm terrified of squirrels.

22
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:28,380
Squirrels?

23
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,780
Well, there'd have to be pine trees first, right?

24
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,660
Well, obviously. You don't have to tell me that.

25
00:02:34,120 --> 00:02:36,510
Sis, hurry up and come see! It's so beautiful up here!

26
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,020
Come on!

27
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:37,980
Hurry, hurry!

28
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:04,380
So these are our little cabins!

29
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:07,740
So pretty! Yay! It's gorgeous!

30
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:16,960
Matthew! Teddy! Come check this out!

31
00:03:28,360 --> 00:03:29,340
Matthew, get up here!

32
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:30,780
This is our dorm room!

33
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:34,140
Teddy, what do you think of our room?

34
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:35,100
Matthew!

35
00:03:50,620 --> 00:03:51,420
Mark!

36
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:52,380
Lead everyone inside

37
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:53,340
and put your things in your rooms.

38
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:55,380
I've gotta go see Manager Ma about something.

39
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:58,790
Alright, everyone, head back to your rooms
and rest up for half an hour.

40
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:02,460
In 30 minutes, we'll all meet up at the dining hall.

41
00:04:02,720 --> 00:04:05,340
And this afternoon, we'll begin our hellish training!

42
00:04:05,800 --> 00:04:08,220
Wait, training this afternoon? If we train that hard,

43
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:10,620
aren't we the ones who'll end up turning into devils?

44
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:13,020
Yeah, well, I think you're already halfway there.

45
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:16,400
Alright, dismissed.

46
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:29,820
The Runner-Up from America.

47
00:04:30,280 --> 00:04:31,740
We were all so impressed back there.

48
00:04:33,640 --> 00:04:35,100
But I just gotta ask...

49
00:04:35,560 --> 00:04:37,020
how come the Champion didn't show up?

50
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:41,820
Who even knows what that small time California Tournament

51
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,260
in America is actually like?

52
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,620
Maybe there were only 2 people competing in total!

53
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:49,500
You guys shouldn't say that.

54
00:04:51,400 --> 00:04:52,380
Leo's Runner-Up title is legit.

55
00:04:52,840 --> 00:04:54,300
I saw it with my own eyes.

56
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,220
Oh, and how exactly did you see it?

57
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:59,100
I... well, I saw it in a photo.

58
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:01,020
A photo? Please.

59
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:03,420
Nowadays, with Photoshop,

60
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:05,340
any photo can be faked!

61
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:09,180
Alright, let's not blindly worship foreign idols anymore.

62
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,020
If he really was some Runner-Up from America,

63
00:05:13,760 --> 00:05:15,420
he should have a match against our Captain.

64
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:19,230
Sorry.

65
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:21,660
I'm here to train. I'm not interested in a private match.

66
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:29,820
Hmph. What an attitude.

67
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:32,220
Too scared to compete? He's just making excuses.

68
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:37,500
Alright, let's go unpack our stuff.

69
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:49,020
Wow, not bad.

70
00:05:52,840 --> 00:05:54,300
Mini, this closet is way too small.

71
00:05:54,760 --> 00:05:55,740
I don't think your clothes are gonna fit.

72
00:05:56,680 --> 00:05:57,180
No worries.

73
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:08,190
Mini, you don't have that much luggage.

74
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:09,180
Just putting it here is fine.

75
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:10,980
It's okay. I can put it anywhere.

76
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:34,920
Mini, let me tell you.

77
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,060
Leo must be thinking

78
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,980
about our beautiful encounter too.

79
00:06:40,840 --> 00:06:43,170
Really? Did you ask him?

80
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:44,670
Do I even need to ask?

81
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:46,590
I can tell just by the way he looks at me.

82
00:06:48,520 --> 00:06:49,500
I'm gonna shower first!

83
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:13,500
The water pressure is so low, and the showerhead is awful.

84
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:15,900
The hardest thing to endure in life is

85
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:17,820
when the shower water pressure is this weak.

86
00:08:47,940 --> 00:08:49,020
This is something I put together myself.

87
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,460
"The Yo-Yo Training Secrets Manual."

88
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:52,380
Everyone, please read this carefully.

89
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:55,740
Whoa, there's actually a secret manual?

90
00:08:57,640 --> 00:08:58,140
You may call it a Manual,

91
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,060
but it's really just my own summary

92
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:01,980
of Fundamental Yo-Yo Skills Training.

93
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:05,820
And in the back, there's a detailed daily schedule.

94
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,700
We have to run in the morning?

95
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,000
That's right.

96
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,280
Training requires a ton of physical stamina.

97
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,940
After the run, we'll move on to fundamental skill drills.

98
00:09:15,400 --> 00:09:16,650
In the afternoon, we'll work on basic Yo-Yo techniques.

99
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:21,660
And in the evening, you'll work on
your own summer homework assignments.

100
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,860
Coach! Where's my copy?

101
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:34,140
I know I printed out 8 copies.
How can there not be enough?

102
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:43,260
Shawn.

103
00:09:47,500 --> 00:09:48,500
Coach...

104
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:57,180
Shawn! Just give me a break, will you? Please!

105
00:09:58,120 --> 00:10:00,540
You were always following me around back at school.

106
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,460
You even followed me to the bathroom!

107
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:05,820
And now you've popped up here, too?

108
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:07,740
How did you even get here?

109
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:10,140
Coach Tony, don't worry about how I got here.

110
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:11,880
Just let me join you guys!

111
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
No thanks.

112
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:16,380
Joining the school Team is a very serious matter.

113
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Ok?

114
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:19,740
Stop clinging to me like a vine!

115
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:23,100
No, no, I'm not. I'm just following, not clinging!

116
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:24,540
Alright, alright.

117
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:26,460
I can't reason with you.

118
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:28,860
Your fundamentals are just too weak.

119
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:32,000
You wouldn't be able to keep up with our training pace.
Don't you get that?

120
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:35,100
Then how about I just watch from the sidelines?
How's that?

121
00:10:35,560 --> 00:10:37,020
Coach Tony, listen to me.

122
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:40,380
I've been exploring, constantly seeking deeper understanding.

123
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:42,300
Right now,

124
00:10:42,760 --> 00:10:44,700
I'm right on the verge of a massive breakthrough!

125
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:47,580
I truly believe that under your guidance, my talent

126
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:50,460
will bubble up and erupt just like boiling water!

127
00:10:50,620 --> 00:10:51,900
Bursting forth with unstoppable energy!

128
00:10:58,120 --> 00:10:59,100
We're on a very tight budget.

129
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:02,460
We can't afford to cover your living expenses here.
Do you understand?

130
00:11:02,920 --> 00:11:05,820
Coach, I've got my own money. I won't be a burden on you.

131
00:11:07,040 --> 00:11:08,700
Look, I know the money for this Training Camp

132
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:10,140
will only last for 2 weeks.

133
00:11:15,400 --> 00:11:16,860
How do you know that?

134
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:19,740
You cannot tell anyone about this.

135
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,660
Don't tell a single soul, got it?

136
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:24,540
No, I won't. I promise. I'll just train with you guys.

137
00:11:25,000 --> 00:11:25,500
I'll do anything.

138
00:11:30,760 --> 00:11:33,180
Suit yourself. Be my guest.

139
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:39,900
Heh. That was way too easy.

140
00:11:52,700 --> 00:12:02,000
1,2,3,4!

141
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:04,860
Go, Jianghai Team!

142
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:07,260
Jianghai Team, all the way!

143
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:10,140
Jianghai Team, let's go!

144
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Come on!

145
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Coach, I can't stand it.

146
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:28,980
You two are 3 laps behind already!

147
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,000
Ah!

148
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:32,220
Shawn, what are you doing?!

149
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,580
I'm absorbing the essence of the Earth!

150
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:37,000
What?

151
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:40,350
The Earth is like a giant carton of yogurt.

152
00:12:41,800 --> 00:12:45,180
And this tree trunk is the perfect giant straw.

153
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:47,100
Wow, so poetic!

154
00:12:48,040 --> 00:12:50,460
You lunatic! You're clinging to that tree like a Koala!

155
00:12:50,920 --> 00:12:52,270
You scared us half to death! You call that poetry?

156
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:54,780
What's going on?

157
00:12:58,880 --> 00:12:59,580
Keep training!

158
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:31,260
Sis, I can't run anymore.

159
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:33,960
We came all this way just to run?

160
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:35,580
This is so boring.

161
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:40,860
Look at Leo over there. He's still going strong.

162
00:13:42,060 --> 00:13:43,330
Don't tell me he wants to be Captain?

163
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:46,620
Him? Please.

164
00:13:47,360 --> 00:13:48,540
He's no match for Mark.

165
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,940
You guys shouldn't always be badmouthing
people behind their backs.

166
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:54,300
What does a little kid know? Stop interrupting adults.

167
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:57,180
I'm not a kid! I'm your Teammate now!

168
00:13:58,120 --> 00:13:59,100
Teammate?

169
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:00,060
You really think

170
00:14:00,120 --> 00:14:01,500
you're good enough to be my Teammate?

171
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:02,570
If it weren't for Mark,

172
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:06,300
Forget it.

173
00:14:06,760 --> 00:14:09,180
Explain yourself! Everyone is listening!

174
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:11,100
I made the Team based on my own skills!

175
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:13,020
Stop looking down on people!

176
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:17,260
You're barely taller than a blade of grass,
but you've sure got an attitude.

177
00:14:18,080 --> 00:14:19,940
Don't think you're all that just 'cause you're tall.

178
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,180
You still lost to Leo!

179
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:23,100
Say that again.

180
00:14:23,360 --> 00:14:24,540
I'm just stating the facts.

181
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,940
If you've got the guts, have him face me again.

182
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,380
Then you'll see what the facts are.

183
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,820
Hmph. Forget it.

184
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:31,740
Tonight, I'll settle this with you once and for all.

185
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,140
Mickey, don't cause trouble.

186
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,100
Sis, stay out of this.

187
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:36,540
According to the rules,

188
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,940
you're supposed to be doing your homework tonight.

189
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:43,740
Remember, you brought it on yourself, little squirt.

190
00:14:56,760 --> 00:14:58,620
What's wrong? Can't wait any longer?

191
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:01,500
I'm busy tonight.

192
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,900
Or maybe you just don't want your sister to find out

193
00:15:04,060 --> 00:15:05,340
how badly you're gonna lose.

194
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:06,890
We'll see who loses.

195
00:15:07,720 --> 00:15:08,220
I'm warning you.

196
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:11,100
Leo's gonna get kicked off the Team sooner or later.

197
00:15:12,220 --> 00:15:14,460
Sticking with Mark is your only way out.

198
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:15,900
What's it to you?

199
00:15:17,800 --> 00:15:19,690
I don't wanna waste my breath.
Let's just get this over with.

200
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Good.

201
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:23,100
Then let's do "Lightning Fast" 30 times.

202
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:25,500
Fine, don't expect me to go easy.

203
00:15:36,700 --> 00:15:40,500
[Name: Mickey | Team: Jianghai]
[Yo-Yo: Ferris Wheel | Special Move: Ferris Flying Saucer]

204
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:47,400
[Name: Matthew | Team: Jianghai]
[Yo-Yo: Shockwave | Special Move: Phantom Shockwave]

205
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:16,860
Done.

206
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:23,580
Sorry, but I did "Lightning Fast" 35 times.

207
00:16:24,040 --> 00:16:25,020
I win.

208
00:16:25,480 --> 00:16:25,980
See ya.

209
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,300
You little punk.

210
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,750
Speed isn't absolute.

211
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:12,060
It's relative.

212
00:17:48,040 --> 00:17:49,020
Jianghai Team, fall in!

213
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:00,060
Rise and shine!

214
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:02,430
What's going on?

215
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:03,870
Get up, come on, hurry!

216
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,820
It's only been 2 days! Are you made of paper or what?

217
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:07,710
Teddy, move it!

218
00:18:07,720 --> 00:18:09,180
Chuck! Chuck, get up!

219
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:13,020
Mickey! Mickey, get up!

220
00:18:13,480 --> 00:18:14,940
Leo! Leo, come on!

221
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:16,860
Stop sleeping!

222
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:26,940
Where is everyone?

223
00:18:28,840 --> 00:18:31,100
Popcorn, hurry up! We're gonna be late again!

224
00:18:32,200 --> 00:18:34,140
What's the rush? I haven't even put on my sunscreen yet!

225
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,310
Alright, alright, let's go!

226
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:37,500
Why are you so excited?

227
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,220
Don't hold it too high.

228
00:18:46,120 --> 00:18:47,100
Parallel to your face.

229
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:50,460
Watch it, not too high.

230
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:58,140
Keep your eyes locked on the egg.

231
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:01,020
That's it. Eyes on it, hand to it.

232
00:19:05,320 --> 00:19:08,700
Don't hold your hand up so high. Relax, relax.

233
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:11,580
Only lift it slightly when you
flick your wrist. Pay attention.

234
00:19:17,320 --> 00:19:19,740
Alright, everyone.

235
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,140
What you're practicing today

236
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:24,230
is from The Yo-Yo Training Secrets Manual.

237
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:27,420
Chapter 1. The most fundamental exercise.

238
00:19:27,880 --> 00:19:28,860
Don't underestimate this drill.

239
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:32,740
It'll strengthen your fingers, wrists, and arms.

240
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:35,180
Your sense of rhythm and coordination, too.

241
00:19:36,040 --> 00:19:37,470
Catching the egg trains your accuracy

242
00:19:37,900 --> 00:19:39,000
when you recall the Yo-Yo.

243
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:41,340
This is actually a scoring component in Competition.

244
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:45,180
I know today's drill might feel a bit tedious.

245
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:48,540
But these are the most essential fundamental exercises.

246
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:50,940
There will be many more drills like this to come.

247
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,820
We'll be introducing them step by step.

248
00:19:54,280 --> 00:19:56,810
Now we'll do the brick hanging drill. Everyone get ready.

249
00:19:58,120 --> 00:19:59,100
Keep your arm balanced.

250
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:10,620
Hold it!

251
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:13,500
Hold it! Hold on!

252
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:16,380
Keep it up

253
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:18,780
Matthew, good.

254
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:21,970
Monica, focus!

255
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:28,860
I can't take it!

256
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:30,750
I'm dying here!

257
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:32,700
Coach, when do we actually get to practice with the Yo-Yo?

258
00:20:35,080 --> 00:20:37,640
Practice tricks without the fundamentals?
You'll end up with nothing.

259
00:20:39,580 --> 00:20:40,380
Let me say it again.

260
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:43,260
If you want your Yo-Yo to have more power in motion,

261
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:44,700
you have to strengthen

262
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:46,140
the muscles in your middle finger

263
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:48,060
and your wrist.

264
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:51,650
It's only been 2 minutes, and you're already done?

265
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:53,340
Look at Mark's crew.

266
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:59,100
Whoa, Chuck's actually killing it!

267
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:03,420
